{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1497971-at-what-point-do-heptagram-students-become-sorcerers","id":1497971,"title":"At what point do Heptagram students become sorcerers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-24T03:10:48-08:00","id":1497971,"title":"At what point do Heptagram students become sorcerers?","content":"When do young terrestrial students of the Heptagram gain their Shaping Ritual and learn actual Spells?<br /> Assume a series takes place at the Heptagram with characters who are Just Hatched, do they begin with Terrestrial Circle Sorcery or should it be gained through the series?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T06:28:34-08:00","id":1497990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1497971-at-what-point-do-heptagram-students-become-sorcerers#post1497971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When do young terrestrial students of the Heptagram gain their Shaping Ritual and learn actual Spells?<br /> Assume a series takes place at the Heptagram with characters who are Just Hatched, do they begin with Terrestrial Circle Sorcery or should it be gained through the series?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Usually through the series i would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T03:01:29-07:00","id":1507568,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reckoning this out for a Heptagram game I'm running, and it would depend on the character concept, although as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> says, most will learn it over the course of the game itself.<br /> <br /> The current exception in my game* is a Cynis who had his initiation early, and is now quite frightened of his newfound power, and is plunging into whatever drugs he can get his hands on as a coping mechanism for his worldview being shattered. He's been shunted into the Heptagram because the family wants him to learn how to use what he's got, rather than just write him off. His hesitance and lack of expertise in actually using his abilities is why he'll be starting at Year 1 of the Heptagram's programme, rather than getting advanced a year for being a prodigy who's already had his initiation.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a bit of exceptionalism going on here, but the player is new to Exalted, so I want to run with the concepts they present, rather than saying &quot;no, he'll just be pushed into a minor school somewhere and forgotten about&quot;, which is probably what would happen to this sort of character to my mind if they weren't a PC.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *this may change when part 2 of session zero is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T04:44:39-07:00","id":1507577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1497971-at-what-point-do-heptagram-students-become-sorcerers?p=1507568#post1507568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently reckoning this out for a Heptagram game I'm running, and it would depend on the character concept, although as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">Baaldam</a> says, most will learn it over the course of the game itself.<br /> <br /> The current exception in my game* is a Cynis who had his initiation early, and is now quite frightened of his newfound power, and is plunging into whatever drugs he can get his hands on as a coping mechanism for his worldview being shattered. He's been shunted into the Heptagram because the family wants him to learn how to use what he's got, rather than just write him off. His hesitance and lack of expertise in actually using his abilities is why he'll be starting at Year 1 of the Heptagram's programme, rather than getting advanced a year for being a prodigy who's already had his initiation.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is a bit of exceptionalism going on here, but the player is new to Exalted, so I want to run with the concepts they present, rather than saying &quot;no, he'll just be pushed into a minor school somewhere and forgotten about&quot;, which is probably what would happen to this sort of character to my mind if they weren't a PC.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No problem with PCs having unusual circunstances on occasion - it's part &amp; parcel of being among protagonists in a story at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> But now on to some of the character's specifics:<br /> <br /> - What kind of sorcerous initiation did he get and how did that process lead into his current traumatized state - a dalliance with a 2nd Circle demon, being taken through alien vistas by one of the potentates of chaos, a bad trip beyond compare into glimpses of family secrets and withered seeds of ancient blood legacies bloom into eerie new life within him through an exotic mixture of drugs with far more to it than mere entertainment?<br /> <br /> - What sort of shaping rituals or associated merits compose his sorcerous initiation, canon or homebrew? Have you worked on at least some aspects of it with the player?<br /> <br /> - The fact he was mentally unprepared for the process is a pretty good indicator that he went at it on its own, with no (responsible) tutors to guide him, how did it happen in the first place. Someone lent him necessary materials or he obtained them on its lonesome self with no inkling of the risks or consequences - some long-forgotten jewel or tome of esoteric lore of a blasphemous nature lost amidst spot clean but unused bookshelves or trophy cases untouched in centuries, the skull of a fallen nemesis of one's ancestors with far more to it than suspected?<br /> <br /> - What part of the Blessed Isle or Threshold does he come from and who did he live with before the move to the Isle of Voices? Sketching out his immediate family/household and their reactions to the whole mess might be of good use in the future.<br /> <br /> - What is his control spell and how have its effects changed or disrupted his past lifestyle - in fact, how does the move away from home or primary education and into academy life change the kind of routine he was used to?<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, you might want to look into NPCs across the books for some additional sample sorcerous initiations, rituals or related artifacts as sources of inspiration on the kind of strangeness one may bump into across the many varied corners of Creation. Ifraja the Librarian (from Adversaries of the Righteous) has a very interesting example of what could be considered a blasphemous artifact book of sorcerous lore. The artifact weapon Asphodel in Arms of the Chosen is another great canon example of a possible stealth tutor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-17-2024, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T05:27:39-07:00","id":1507861,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, were I running a Heptagram student game, I'd probably say advanced Occult and Lore, as well as your Initiation and your control spell the first year (failing out if you don't initiate), then Shaping Rituals, Sorcerous Merits, and your first non-control spells second year. By the end of third year your first Working, taking the place of something like a Master's thesis. From there it's back to your family, a stint with the Legions or Wyld Hunt, or maybe you do some post-graduate work in advanced Workings, Artifact crafting, or Manse design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T00:12:26-07:00","id":1508714,"title":"","content":"Your first Working, which functions similarly to a Master's thesis, is due at the end of your third year. Returning to your family, joining the Legions or Wyld Hunt, or continuing your education with additional courses in Workings, Artifact crafting, or Manse design are all possible next steps.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><a href=\"https://puppethockey.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">puppet hockey</span></a></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27673-manisla","name":"Manisla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T03:33:13-07:00","id":1508873,"title":"","content":"I am in the process of planning out a Heptagram game and for my table it will depend on the character and what the player wants. The minimum requirement for graduating the Heptagram is Occult 3 and the Sorcery charm. The character can start out with sorcery if that is what they want, or they can learn it in game. I am assuming that most characters will have picked it up by year 3, but am not making this a hard requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:03:14-07:00","id":1508901,"title":"","content":"It should be recalled that, in this Edition, there is no standard curriculum for the Heptagram, it's rather a set of resources and qualified instructors that students can go to as necessary while pursuing their own inquiry into the occult.<br /> <br /> This would align it with the current presentation of sorcery, in which the processes for acquiring it are varied, esoteric, deeply personal, and not actually suitable to all Exalted. It is text that not all who spend their full seven years at the Heptagram actually initiate into sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-19-2023, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}